.\" Manual page for the ALEPH-M tools: acomp, aopt, alink, jslink
.TH ALEPH-M 1 "November 2026" "ALEPH-M v2.5" "ALEPH-M tools"
.SH NAME
acomp, aopt, alink, jslink \- compile, optimize and link ALEPH programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acomp
.RI [ options ]
.IR file " ..."
.br
.B aopt
.RB [ \-no\-rule ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.I input
.br
.B alink
.RI [ options ]
.IR file " ..."
.br
.B jslink
.RI [ options ]
.IR file " ..."
.PP
Each program also accepts
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version .
.SH DESCRIPTION
An ALEPH program consists of a main program and any number of modules,
each in its own source file with extension
.BR .ale .
Building a program takes three steps.
.TP
.B acomp
compiles one source file (a main program or a module) into an
intermediate file with extension
.BR .ice .
The .ice file is a readable text; among others it contains every rule as
a graph of calls with success and failure continuations.
.TP
.B aopt
optimizes an .ice file: removes entries which are not used, and merges
identical nodes in the rule graphs.
This step is optional.
.TP
.B alink
links the .ice files of the main program, of all modules, and of the
standard library into a single C program, to be compiled by a C compiler
together with the files of the runtime core.
.TP
.B jslink
does the same as
.BR alink ,
but generates a JavaScript program, which runs on top of the JavaScript
runtime environment
.BR alephRE.js .
.PP
The word size is 32 bits for both targets.
.SH ACOMP
The file arguments are source files; the extension
.B .ale
can be omitted.
Usually a single source file is given, modules are compiled
separately.
Modules mentioned in
.B require
and
.B library
pragmats (see
.B Other options
below) are read but are not compiled as only their public parts are used.
.SS Global options
A later option of the same kind replaces an earlier one.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
The output file; the extension
.B .ice
is added.
Without this option the name is derived from the first source file, and
the output is written to the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-I " dir" : dir...
Colon separated list of directories searched for
.B require
and
.B include
source files.
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
The directory containing the standard library source
.BR stdlib.ale .
The default search path is
.BR ./aleph:/usr/local/aleph .
.SS Local options
These are reset after each source file.
.TP
.B \-W
Set the warning level to 3; the default is 4 (and 6 while reading
library modules).
Warnings below the warning level are not shown.
.TP
.B \-Wall
Set the warning level to 0: show all warnings.
.TP
.B \-l
Print the program text
.RB ( list=on ).
.TP
.B \-d
Print the dictionary of tag occurrences
.RB ( dictionary=on ).
.SS Other options
.TP
.BI \-D " tag"
Same as the pragmat
.BI define= tag\fR.
.TP
.BI \-m " file"
Same as the pragmat
.BI require=\(dq file \(dq\fR.
.TP
.BI \-y " file"
Same as the pragmat
.BI library=\(dq file \(dq\fR:
process
.I file
as a user library.
.TP
.BI \-\- name = value
Processed as
.BI 'pragmat' name = value\fR.
.PP
If there are errors, no .ice file is written.
.SH AOPT
.TP
.I input
The .ice file to be optimized; the extension can be omitted.
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Write the optimized code to
.IR output .
Without this option
.I input
is replaced by the optimized code.
.TP
.B \-no\-rule
Remove unused entries only; do not optimize the rule graphs.
.SH ALINK
The file arguments are the .ice files of the main program and of all
modules it requires, in any order; the extension can be omitted.
Exactly one of them must be a main program.
The standard library is added automatically.
.TP
.BI \-o " target"
The output file; the extension
.B .c
is added.
Without this option the name of the main .ice file is used, and the
output is written to the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
The directory containing the precompiled standard library
.BR stdC.ice .
The default search path is
.BR ./aleph/stdice:/usr/local/aleph .
.TP
.B \-no\-stdlib
Do not add the standard library.
.TP
.B \-W
Report public items which are not used.
.TP
.B \-g
Link with call stack information, used by the library rule
.B backtrack
and in the report printed when the program is aborted.
.PP
Constant expressions, list sizes, virtual addresses and classification
areas are evaluated and checked by the linker, thus errors in them are
reported at this stage.
The generated C file is compiled together with the runtime core, for
example
.PP
.nf
.RS
gcc \-O2 \-I coreC \-o prog prog.c coreC/*.c
.RE
.fi
.SH JSLINK
The file arguments and the options
.BR \-o ,
.BR \-L ,
.BR \-no\-stdlib ,
.BR \-W ,
and
.B \-g
are the same as for
.BR alink ,
with the following differences.
The extension of the output file is
.BR .js ;
the precompiled standard library is
.BR stdjs.ice .
.TP
.B \-no\-async
Do not generate asynchronous calls.
By default the generated code is asynchronous, so that the program can
wait for input, e.g., from a console, without blocking.
.TP
.BI \-\-RE= file
The name of the runtime library script the generated program loads; the
default is
.BR alephRE.js .
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile the main program
.B prog.ale
and the module
.BR mod.ale ,
link them, and build the executable:
.PP
.nf
.RS
acomp \-I stdlib \-o work/prog prog
acomp \-I stdlib \-o work/mod mod
aopt work/prog
aopt work/mod
alink \-L stdC \-o work/prog work/prog work/mod
gcc \-O2 \-I coreC \-o work/prog work/prog.c coreC/*.c
.RE
.fi
.PP
Link the same .ice files into a JavaScript program:
.PP
.nf
.RS
jslink \-L stdjs \-o work/prog.js work/prog work/mod
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compile with all warnings and with a program listing:
.PP
.nf
.RS
acomp \-Wall \-l \-I stdlib prog
.RE
.fi
.SH RUNNING THE PROGRAM
Command line arguments of a compiled C program are available to the
ALEPH program in the list
.BR STDARG .
If the program was compiled with the pragmat
.BR trace=on ,
tracing output is printed only when the first argument is
.BR \-T .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B stdlib.ale
source of the standard library heads, read by
.B acomp
.TP
.B stdC.ice
compiled standard library for the C target, read by
.B alink
.TP
.B stdjs.ice
compiled standard library for the JavaScript target, read by
.B jslink
.TP
.B coreC/
C sources and header files of the runtime core
.TP
.B corejs/alephRE.js
JavaScript runtime environment
